### care-pathway-service — example requests
# care-pathway/care-pathway-service-with-loco — loco-idiomatic layout
# (src/controllers/). Envelope: BARE loco JSON, same posture as
# organization.http — see that file's header for the full explanation.
# Gated by CARE_PATHWAY_REQUIRE_AUTH (default off). No REST bulk
# import/export in this crate (only FHIR $export, near the bottom).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8088
@pathwayPid = REPLACE_WITH_PID_FROM_CREATE
# curl-verified example: creating the body below in a local run produced
# pid 448813be-ebb1-43c4-bbd8-589c0b79277f — copy your own create
# response's "pid" instead of reusing this one.
@instancePid = REPLACE_WITH_PID_FROM_INSTANCE_CREATE
# curl-verified: enrolling a subject via POST .../instances (below)
# produces a response with its own "pid" — copy that in, distinct from
# the pathway's own pid above.
@token = REPLACE_WITH_BEARER_FROM_00-auth-handshake.http


### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/_health


### Who am I — always requires a valid bearer token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/care-pathways/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Create a care pathway — minimal valid body.
# curl-verified response: {"pid":"<uuid>","name":"Acute Stroke Care Pathway"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/care-pathways
Content-Type: application/json
Accepts-version: 1.0

{
  "name": "Acute Stroke Care Pathway",
  "provider_id": "trust-1",
  "pathway_code": "STROKE-01",
  "condition_codes": [{ "system": "Icd10", "code": "I63" }],
  "identifiers": [{ "scheme": "GuidelineId", "value": "NICE-NG128" }]
}


### Get the created care pathway back
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/care-pathways/{{pathwayPid}}


### List — paginated (X-Total-Count / X-Limit / X-Offset headers)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/care-pathways?limit=25&offset=0


### Search — fuzzy + phonetic via Tantivy; condition codes and
# interventions are searchable too.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/care-pathways/search?q=Stroke&fuzzy=true&phonetic=true


### Probabilistic + deterministic match
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/care-pathways/match
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Acute Stroke Care Pathway", "provider_id": "trust-1" }


### Explicit duplicate check
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/care-pathways/check-duplicates
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Acute Stroke Care Pathway" }


### Merge two confirmed-duplicate pathways (destructive)
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/care-pathways/merge
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "main_pid": "{{pathwayPid}}", "duplicate_pid": "<other-uuid>" }


### Directory insight — pathways grouped by care setting / specialty
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/care-pathways/insights/directory


### Enroll a patient into a pathway instance (an operational sub-resource
# distinct from the pathway template itself)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/care-pathways/{{pathwayPid}}/instances
Content-Type: application/json

{ "subject_ref": "person:11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111" }


### Get a pathway instance
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/instances/{{instancePid}}


### Advance a pathway instance to its next step. Body field is `to`, not
# `status` (curl-verified: `{"status":...}` 422s "Bad Request"). Legal
# transitions (src/instances.rs): active <-> on_hold, either -> completed
# or discontinued (terminal).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/instances/{{instancePid}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "to": "on_hold" }


### Masked view (privacy.md)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/care-pathways/{{pathwayPid}}/masked


### GDPR export for a pathway instance's subject
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/care-pathways/{{pathwayPid}}/export


### Audit trail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/care-pathways/{{pathwayPid}}/audit


### FHIR R5 — read this pathway as a PlanDefinition resource
GET {{baseUrl}}/fhir/PlanDefinition/{{pathwayPid}}


### FHIR Bulk Data — kick off an async $export (ONC/HTI-style bulk
# export; this crate's compliance reference implementation). GET, not
# POST (curl-verified: POST 405s); mounted at /fhir/$export, NOT under
# /fhir/PlanDefinition/$export. curl-verified: 202 Accepted with a
# Content-Location header pointing at the status-poll URL.
GET {{baseUrl}}/fhir/$export


### Delete (soft-delete) a care pathway
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/care-pathways/{{pathwayPid}}
